# File: tests/features/add_greeting_nfkd_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/358-add-greeting-nfkd-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the completed greeting in Unicode NFKD

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Fold compatibility characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkd is called with U+FB01 ona, fullwidth A da, and Ada superscript two
    Then the results are Hello, fiona with 12 code points, Hello, Ada with 10 code points, and Hello, Ada2 with 11 code points
    And each result is a str

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Decompose precomposed characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkd is called with precomposed Chloé
    Then the result is Hello, Chloe plus U+0301 with 13 code points

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Leave already-normalized text unchanged
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkd is called with Ada, Ada two-spaces Lovelace, and Chloe plus U+0301
    Then each result equals greet of the same name

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Agree with unicodedata NFKD
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkd is called with Ada, precomposed Chloé, U+FB01 ona, and O'Brien-Smith
    Then each result equals unicodedata NFKD normalization of greet of the same name
    And each result is NFKD-normalized

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_nfkd is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_nfkd of U+FB01 ona
    Then it prints Hello, fiona and greeting_nfkd is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the NFKD rule and the inherited invalid-name error
